<pending_commit branch="arc-12.1.0-pre2" change_id="Ia1cb9154b59e19e02a75de9642fbad7adeadbeef" commit="d79858658cc9b76d66babb63ef5e8f6c0842d094" commit_message="Revert &quot;CHROMIUM: egl: Add missing flags for Android builds&quot;  This reverts commit e3d6048ad7c38a4226af381caa16edf5b88619ac.  We don't need drm_gralloc libs and flags anymore, and we can also use pkgconfig to get the other libraries.  BUG=b/32077475 TEST=arc-mesa-compiles  CQ-DEPEND=CL:404151, CL:403315  Change-Id: Ia1cb9154b59e19e02a75de9642fbad7adeadbeef Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/404150 Commit-Ready: Gurchetan Singh &lt;gurchetansingh@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Gurchetan Singh &lt;gurchetansingh@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Tomasz Figa &lt;tfiga@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="404150" owner_email="gurchetansingh@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/third_party/mesa" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/mesa" ref="refs/changes/50/404150/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="arc-12.1.0-pre2" change_id="I629d7b2d1a40dca376a0c7ada550dbe0325b5f91" commit="31820ddf9fa4deece6c2e8560b6de52b6a9ab2fd" commit_message="FROMLIST: configure.ac: Don't look for pthreads in Android platform  In Android, the pthreads libs are in bionic.  When building Mesa for Android with the autotools workflow, we shouldn't set -lpthread or -pthread.  BUG=b/32077475 TEST=arc-mesa-compiles CQ-DEPEND=CL:403315, CL:404150  Change-Id: I629d7b2d1a40dca376a0c7ada550dbe0325b5f91 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/404151 Commit-Ready: Gurchetan Singh &lt;gurchetansingh@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Gurchetan Singh &lt;gurchetansingh@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Tomasz Figa &lt;tfiga@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="404151" owner_email="gurchetansingh@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="6" project="chromiumos/third_party/mesa" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/mesa" ref="refs/changes/51/404151/6" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="arc-12.1.0-pre2" change_id="Ia1cb9154b59e19e02a75de9642fbad7a440d54cc" commit="8fb1fb848c3a71d9287913b7a0922aa429344e5a" commit_message="FROMLIST: egl: Use pkg-config for Android NDK build  It's possible to build Mesa for Android using the traditional autotools workflow [1]. ChromiumOS fetches Android prebuilts and puts them in a sysroot. We now want to use pkg-config to specify the location of system headers and libraries [2].  To enable this, let's add the required pkg-config checks and link against them.  [1] https://developer.android.com/ndk/guides/standalone_toolchain.html [2] https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/#/c/403237/  v2: Bundle pkg-config checks together (Emil) v3: Provide further context on standalone NDK Mesa build (Emil)  BUG=b/32077475 TEST=arc-mesa builds  CQ-DEPEND=CL:403237, CL:404150, CL:404151  Change-Id: Ia1cb9154b59e19e02a75de9642fbad7a440d54cc Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/403315 Commit-Ready: Gurchetan Singh &lt;gurchetansingh@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Gurchetan Singh &lt;gurchetansingh@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Tomasz Figa &lt;tfiga@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="403315" owner_email="gurchetansingh@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="7" project="chromiumos/third_party/mesa" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/mesa" ref="refs/changes/15/403315/7" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I7d0538dc09109d1deaeb584e61ee9febf4b5f902" commit="36f44909aabb29eb1e3addbaca087ea810548eec" commit_message="arc-build: add pkgconfig-arc to help build arc-mesa  Upstream wants the Android libs that are required when building arc-mesa to be found using pkg-config.  To do this, let's create the .pc files we need and put them in the Android sysroot. In addition, we need another version of pkg-config for amd64 Android builds.  BUG=b:32077475 TEST=emerge-cyan arc-mesa succeeds CQ-DEPEND=CL:403315  Change-Id: I7d0538dc09109d1deaeb584e61ee9febf4b5f902 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/403237 Commit-Ready: Gurchetan Singh &lt;gurchetansingh@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Gurchetan Singh &lt;gurchetansingh@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Tomasz Figa &lt;tfiga@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="403237" owner_email="gurchetansingh@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="9" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/37/403237/9" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I2eb1733429f20e1baceb69f59cf8f971b4d2809f" commit="f598fa23519e7f02225827da8f5ce6af288de292" commit_message="UPSTREAM: linux-firmware: rockchip: update dptx firmware to v3.1  This version firmware resolved HBR2 Compliance Test failed, and improved compatibility by adjusting the phy configuration. Improved stability of HDCP.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:55030, chrome-os-partner:56523 TEST=check the DP display  Change-Id: I2eb1733429f20e1baceb69f59cf8f971b4d2809f Signed-off-by: Chris Zhong &lt;zyw@rock-chips.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Kyle McMartin &lt;kyle@kernel.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/413163 Reviewed-by: Guenter Roeck &lt;groeck@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="413163" owner_email="zyw@rock-chips.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/linux-firmware" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/linux-firmware" ref="refs/changes/63/413163/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I0b75f26cc91d8f9676ffb77681a9f3afbe49f241" commit="26e958ad7ee13b1cfa73f5c215cfc7aa3def2504" commit_message="UPSTREAM: rockchip/dptx: update WHENCE to version 3.1  52ef7302 didn't bump it here.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:55030, chrome-os-partner:56523 TEST=check the DP display  Change-Id: I0b75f26cc91d8f9676ffb77681a9f3afbe49f241 Signed-off-by: Kyle McMartin &lt;kyle@kernel.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/413164 Commit-Ready: Chris Zhong &lt;zyw@rock-chips.com&gt; Tested-by: Chris Zhong &lt;zyw@rock-chips.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Guenter Roeck &lt;groeck@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="413164" owner_email="zyw@rock-chips.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/linux-firmware" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/linux-firmware" ref="refs/changes/64/413164/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I8b54e93b320e3ea74fc3d6ea13f0d178f9c449cd" commit="07301704df2a8883a20af5fffadf158cdca3330f" commit_message="npcx: hwtimer: Add consecutive reading for ITCNT32  The mux for selecting source clock of ITIM will introduce a delay and have a chance to make ITIM's source clock and core clock are asynchronous. We need consecutive reading for ITCNT32 no matter source clock is APB2 or 32k.  Modified sources: 1. hwtimer.c: Add consecutive reading for ITCNT32  BRANCH=none BUG=chrome-os-partner:34346,chrome-os-partner:59240 TEST=No time stamp symptoms occur on wheatley for 30 hours.  Change-Id: I8b54e93b320e3ea74fc3d6ea13f0d178f9c449cd Signed-off-by: Mulin Chao &lt;mlchao@nuvoton.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/412505 Reviewed-by: Randall Spangler &lt;rspangler@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Shawn N &lt;shawnn@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="412505" owner_email="mlchao@nuvoton.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/05/412505/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I26db49855fa408e68769d60df1927e2621a4c92c" commit="f8df1a2396fdf7f8f4433c361dc875203c6dcd25" commit_message="site_utils: Add new GPU PCI IDs to JSON file  Update the JSON file associated with Intel GPU PCI IDs to include new IDs which have been added to upstream Mesa.  These changes are generated by running the update_intel_pci_ids script.  Change the update_intel_pci_ids script to account for branding changes for Braswell PCI IDs.  BUG=None TEST=./update_intel_pci_ids TEST=test_that &lt;ip_address&gt; graphics_Idle TEST=test_that &lt;ip_address&gt; graphics_dEQP.gles3.info  Change-Id: I26db49855fa408e68769d60df1927e2621a4c92c Signed-off-by: Wayne Boyer &lt;wayne.boyer@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/410170 Commit-Ready: Azhar Shaikh &lt;azhar.shaikh@intel.com&gt; Tested-by: Russ Sage &lt;russ.sage@intel.com&gt; Tested-by: Michael W Mason &lt;michael.w.mason@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Ilja H. Friedel &lt;ihf@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="2" gerrit_number="410170" owner_email="wayne.boyer@intel.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="5" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/70/410170/5" remote="cros" total_fail_count="3"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I8167358a39c9abaf5b62e246fb4c76cc76ecb37f" commit="d582e587cb1074d3193dd79946354dead0f67461" commit_message="CRAS: server_metrics - Fix a bug in sending message  The length in the message header should be length of the message.  BUG=None TEST=use cras_test_client --playback &lt;file&gt; and press p to cause      long delay. After the stream is removed, check debug message      that handler has handle metric message.  Signed-off-by: Cheng-Yi Chiang &lt;cychiang@chromium.org&gt; Change-Id: I8167358a39c9abaf5b62e246fb4c76cc76ecb37f Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/411742 Reviewed-by: Dylan Reid &lt;dgreid@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="411742" owner_email="cychiang@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/adhd" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/adhd" ref="refs/changes/42/411742/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I3f79b02cdf77ac61cf1361033c489604dcd603f2" commit="8b6f5f9ecca3ca58f59fb619c43bafa425880d6b" commit_message="utility: Allow chromeos-tpm-recovery to return failure.  When some of the space re-creation procedure failed, chromeos-tpm-recovery should exit with non-zero value and not saying TPM is successfully recovered.  However, there are few known issues:  - 0x1009 is not needed in TPM2.  - The space is not created in TPM2.  - tlcl does not support define spaces with policies yet (crosbug.com/p/59594).  As a result, we want to return failure only if writing any of the two spaces (0x1007, 0x1008) fails.  This change also revised chromeos-tpm-recovery so it won't exit with unbound variable error due to early exit without having daemon_was_running variable.  BRANCH=None BUG=chrome-os-partner:60099 TEST=For boards with TPM and TPM2, do:      build_image --board $BOARD factory_install;      Boot factory install shim, select 'I' and get TPM recovered.  Change-Id: I3f79b02cdf77ac61cf1361033c489604dcd603f2 Signed-off-by: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/412543 Reviewed-by: Vadim Bendebury &lt;vbendeb@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="412543" owner_email="hungte@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/platform/vboot_reference" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/vboot_reference" ref="refs/changes/43/412543/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-2016.05" change_id="I1382cdf4119fc4eeae5c2b36485030e3a38c2d91" commit="88693836e11266eb29f0d175b58889be31d79aac" commit_message="rockchip/rk3399: display: retry edp initialization if edp initial fail  we found sometime edp get the edid or config video fail on kevin board after reboot. Now we will retry 3 times to initial edp if we found there are error happen in edp initial process.  BRANCH=gru BUG=chrome-os-partner:60150 TEST=reboot on kevin, not found edp initialization error again.  Change-Id: I1382cdf4119fc4eeae5c2b36485030e3a38c2d91 Signed-off-by: Lin Huang &lt;hl@rock-chips.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/412622 Reviewed-by: Julius Werner &lt;jwerner@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="412622" owner_email="hl@rock-chips.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" ref="refs/changes/22/412622/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I2a9ee13117a0bc91710226cd733c5c484c6d0595" commit="e3a50f04b52557375d1d2270da08d568052dfdca" commit_message="g: do not consider valid headers with the 'magic' field corrupted  When cr50 rollback happens, the newer header's magic field is set to zero to prevent it from ever running again.  Take this into consideration when displaying versions of the inactive RW image.  BRANCH=none BUG=none  TEST=loaded two versions of the new code on a cr50 and then modified      the fallback counter to force it to boot the older version and      reboot a Reef. Once Reef fully boots to chrome os examine CR50      version report:       Before:     &gt; vers    ...    RW_A:    0.0.9/DEV/cr50_v1.1.5654-2228b76+    RW_B:  * 0.0.11/DEV/cr50_v1.1.5654-2228b76+    ...      After:     &gt; vers    ...    RW_A:  * 0.0.9/DEV/cr50_v1.1.5654-2228b76+    RW_B:    Error  Change-Id: I2a9ee13117a0bc91710226cd733c5c484c6d0595 Signed-off-by: Vadim Bendebury &lt;vbendeb@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/413089 Reviewed-by: Bill Richardson &lt;wfrichar@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="413089" owner_email="vbendeb@chromiu